      "rating": 5,
      "source": "WeTravel",
      "url": "https://tworldtours.wetravel.com/users/taliya-maya#reviews",
      "destinations": [
        "Zanzibar"
      ],
      "summary": "A first group adventure revealed Zanzibar through food, excursions, shopping, and unexpected moments.",
      "fullText": "This was the trip of a lifetime!! I've never been on a group trip with strangers before, so I reserved my excitement; but if you're booking this location with TWT, it's safe to get excited NOW!\nFrom the moment my feet touched the African soil, I was on the move! Excursions, experiences, shopping, surprises and the most delicious (and authentic) foods! I tend to be a vacationer who doesn't make advanced plans and soaks in the sun every day. This ain't that! And that's what I wanted - someone to take me out of my comfort zone. Taliya did so in a way that was fun, organized and well-thought.\nThe group was so cohesive. Everyone just showed up ready to soak in the experience - no complaints. I don't think you can intentionally plan such a thing with strangers, but we got lucky. About half came with a buddy and half came solo. It was mostly women and mostly black and brown people in their lates 20s thru early 40s. The diversity of location origin, life stages, careers and personality types ensured that everyone could feel welcomed.\nCommunication about the trip is sparce up until about 30 days beforehand. And you'll not be able to chat with other travelers until the trip officially starts. This is by design and works in favor of a more cohesive, trip experience. Taliya and her assistants are available if you have specific questions prior.\nHaving professional photographers capture the moments was a great benefit to me because I was able to not be so attached to my phone when I wanted.\nI was attracted to Zanzibar because of the beautiful, blue water and it did not disappoint! I look back at some of my pictures amazed because it looks like a filter! I did not want this trip to end!! One thing I wish I had known to take advantage of was the opportunity to stay longer on my own time, or the opportunity to go to another country nearby after the trip was over. 6 days will seems very short when you're having as much fun as we had. I recommend stretching it out however you can.",
